---
import InteriorLayout from '@/layouts/InteriorLayout.astro';
import StudioSeal from '@/components/StudioSeal.astro';
import AdinkraIcon from '@/components/AdinkraIcon.astro';
---
<InteriorLayout title="The studio — OhWP Studios" description="An independent technology studio led by Ozzy Hodges in Accra. Software, AI, trading technology, and the craft of building together.">
  <main id="main">
    <section class="interior-mast"><div class="wrap"><div class="about-opening"><div><p class="eyebrow">The studio / Accra, Ghana</p><h1>Good ideas deserve<br /><em>someone who can build.</em></h1><p class="lede">Curiosity across disciplines. Care in every detail. We turn ambitious ideas into useful software — and open the craft to people who want to learn it.</p></div><StudioSeal /></div><div class="mast-foot"><span>A Hodges &amp; Co. studio</span><span>Independent thinking. Hands-on engineering.</span></div></div></section>
    <section class="wrap section-space editorial-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Our story</p><h2>Rooted here.<br />Thinking beyond.</h2><AdinkraIcon symbol="nkyinkyim" size={88} /></div><div class="editorial-copy"><p>OhWP Studios is led by Osborn M. D. K. Hodges — Ozzy — a Ghanaian technologist and founder of Hodges &amp; Co. Limited. The studio brings together practical engineering, considered design, and a belief that technology should make everyday work better.</p><p>Experience across public service, education, commerce, and trading shapes how we build: understand the people first, make the complex feel clear, and deliver something that works in the real world.</p><p>Our Accra roots matter. Mobile money, slow connections, shared devices, and local ways of doing business are design inputs. The ambition travels: thoughtful software for clients here and everywhere.</p><div class="signature"><strong>Ozzy Hodges</strong><span>Founder &amp; hands-on engineer · OhWP Studios</span></div></div></section>
    <section class="interior-band"><div class="wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Two ways to make it happen</p><h2>Built for you.<br /><em>Or built with you.</em></h2><p>Commission a product from idea to launch. Or work alongside us with Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, and GitHub Copilot — learning to scope, build, debug, and ship your own.</p></div><a class="button" href="/contact">Find your way forward <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="wrap section-space"><p class="eyebrow">03 / The practice</p><div class="principle-grid"><article><span class="index">01 — Think broadly</span><h3>A studio for the<br />“could we build…?”</h3><p>Web and mobile products, business platforms, AI tools, integrations, automations, and unfamiliar challenges. We start with the problem and choose the right tools.</p></article><article><span class="index">02 — Build deliberately</span><h3>Proof before<br />promises.</h3><p>Clear scope, working previews, review, and testing. For MetaTrader bots and TradingView indicators across forex, metals, and indices, risk controls and forward testing come first. No grid. No martingale.</p></article><article><span class="index">03 — Share the craft</span><h3>Capability that<br />stays with you.</h3><p>Understand what you own and how to use it. Through guided builds, documentation, and Open Build, we make the decisions behind the software easier to follow.</p><a class="text-link" href="/open-build">Explore Open Build <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article></div></section>
    <section class="interior-band"><div class="wrap"><h2>Bring the idea.<br />Let’s find its shape.</h2><a class="button" href="/contact">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  </main>
</InteriorLayout>
